  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WIPSU</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is implemented in Zimbabwe. The main outcome areas it contributes to is opposing the backlash   increasing gender equality. The main rights holders are women with leadership positions in the wings/assemblies of the political parties represented in Parliament, top leadership/structures of political parties represented in Parliament, selected women Councillors, marginalised and poor women living in target constituencies and Wards led by women Members of Parliament and Councillors- Ward Consultative Forum/Constituency Consultative Forum, selected Parliament of Zimbabwe Portfolio Committees, Provincial Councils, targeted local authorities- chiefs, headmen, local leaders, and officials and selected like-minded civil society organisations including the faith based institutions and labour unions.Through focusing on the structures and norms in varies spheres of the political space the project aims to achieve progressive development within the outcome areas. This will be done by capacity building to rights holders, but also to engage constructively with the institutions and the individual political parties in a non-biased and informed way.</narrative>
  </description>
